    declaration: function-decl #958 33070:582:1-33406:593:1 name="@2::accept_websocket" doc="Checks that `request` is a WebSocket handshake and makes the `Upgrade` that runs `session` on it. The request must\nbe a `GET` with `Upgrade: websocket`, `Connection: Upgrade`, `Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13` and a `Sec-WebSocket-Key`\nof 16 bytes in base64. A request that is not gets an `Upgrade.Reply`: 426 with `Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13` for\nanother version, 400 for the rest. The first of `options.protocols` that the client offers in\n`Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` is agreed on (`WebSocket.protocol`). No extension is accepted, so no frame is compressed.\nThe server does not check `Origin`: a browser sends it with every handshake, and a handler that serves pages of its\nown should compare it with `header_values(request.headers, \"origin\")` before it accepts. It is an `error` when\n`options` is out of range."
      param: param #929 33094:583:3-33119:583:28 name="request"
        type: type-ref #928 33103:583:12-33119:583:28 name="HttpWire.Request"
      param: param #931 33123:584:3-33148:584:28 name="session"
        type: type-ref #930 33132:584:12-33148:584:28 name="@2::WebSocketSession"
      param: param #934 33152:585:3-33198:585:49 name="options"
        type: type-ref #932 33161:585:12-33177:585:28 name="@2::WebSocketOptions"
